# PART 5 — THE MULTI-TENANT ARCHITECTURE

This is one of the most important characteristics of ShieldNet Hub.

ShieldNet Hub is one central platform serving multiple independent developers and estate businesses.

Example:

- Developer A joins ShieldNet Hub and registers three estates.
- Developer B joins and registers two estates.
- Developer C joins and registers five estates.

All participating estates may appear on the same public marketplace.

However, each developer operates within a separate private business workspace.

### Tenant isolation requirements

Each developer must have access only to their authorised business information.

This includes:

- Estates.
- Inventory.
- Staff.
- Buyers.
- Leads.
- Sales.
- Reservations.
- Payments.
- Financial reports.
- Internal documents.
- Operational records.

Where appropriate, records must be associated with developer_id and estate_id.

Use PostgreSQL security mechanisms, backend authorisation and row-level security where appropriate.

Do not rely on hiding frontend menu items as the security mechanism.

### Platform ownership

ShieldNet Technologies owns the reusable platform software, source code, underlying architecture, AI orchestration and reusable product components.

Developers retain their existing property, land, business and customer rights, subject to their agreements.

Platform licensing, commercial rights, commissions, fees and project participation must be separately documented.

