# PART 8 — HOW THE ENTIRE PLATFORM WORKS

The platform must operate as one connected business ecosystem.

Consider this complete workflow:

1. A developer registers on ShieldNet Hub.
2. ShieldNet Super Admin reviews and approves the developer.
3. The developer receives a private business workspace.
4. The developer creates an estate.
5. The developer uploads approved estate information and plot inventory.
6. Approved estate listings become visible on the public marketplace.
7. A visitor discovers the estate.
8. The visitor explores available plots and prices.
9. The visitor submits an enquiry.
10. The enquiry enters the developer's CRM.
11. A sales manager assigns the enquiry to an agent.
12. The agent contacts the prospective buyer.
13. A viewing is scheduled.
14. The buyer requests a reservation.
15. An authorised manager approves or rejects it.
16. Finance records the payment.
17. An authorised officer independently verifies the payment.
18. The system updates the relevant financial records and inventory according to approved business rules.
19. The buyer sees the confirmed transaction in their personal portal.
20. The developer's dashboard reflects the updated business information.

This is the core business journey ShieldNet Hub must support.

