# PART 10 — AI RELIABILITY AND GOVERNANCE

ShieldNet Hub must incorporate an AI Reliability and Governance layer.

This is an important part of the long-term product vision.

## 10.1 Guardrail & Token-Cost Proxy Middleware

Implement a controlled middleware layer to manage:

- AI token usage.
- Cost limits.
- Input validation.
- Output validation.
- Semantic guardrails.
- Tool permission checks.
- Restricted actions.
- Usage monitoring.
- Escalation.
- AI execution logs.

The objective is to protect developers and ShieldNet Technologies from uncontrolled AI usage, unauthorised actions and unnecessary operating costs.

## 10.2 Agent Evaluation & Regression Testing Harness

Build an evaluation system that can test AI agents before deployment and after significant changes.

Test:

- Response accuracy.
- Property retrieval accuracy.
- Lead qualification consistency.
- Tenant isolation.
- Permission compliance.
- Tool execution.
- Financial information handling.
- Hallucination risks.
- Regression failures.
- Cost and token consumption.

Store evaluation results, failure reports and test history.

Agents must not be treated as reliable simply because they produce convincing responses.

